.TH FOXTERM 1 "2026" "FOX 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
foxterm \- FOX terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foxterm
[\fB--profile\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB--term\fR \fIvt100\fR|\fIxterm\fR]
[\fB--working-directory\fR \fIdir\fR]
[\fB--execute\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIarg\fR ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B foxterm
opens a native window with a terminal view. It starts the default shell on a
pseudo terminal and accepts text, keys, mouse reporting, selection and clipboard
operations. The initial implementation uses one tab per window; multiple tabs
and tear-off are added by the terminal workstream.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --profile \fIname\fR
Select a profile. The built-in profile is \fBdefault\fR.
.TP
.B --term \fIvt100\fR|\fIxterm\fR
Select the terminal emulation and TERM value.
.TP
.B --working-directory \fIdir\fR
Start the child in \fIdir\fR.
.TP
.B --execute \fIcommand\fR [\fIarg\fR ...]
Run \fIcommand\fR directly, without a shell.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Show the FOX version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The child inherits the environment and receives
.BR TERM ,
.BR COLUMNS ,
.BR LINES ,
.BR TERM_PROGRAM ,
and, for xterm mode,
.BR COLORTERM .
The default shell is taken from
.B COMSPEC
on Windows and
.B SHELL
on POSIX systems.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fox-config (1)
